ntensive tasks","topics":[],"score":2300},{"name":"saransh2405/bi-gram-word-suggestion","owner":"saransh2405","html_url":"https://github.com/saransh2405/bi-gram-word-suggestion","stars":1,"forks":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"In the fields of computational linguistics and probability, an n-gram is a contiguous sequence of n items from a given sequence of text or speech. The items can be phonemes, syllables, letters, words or base pairs according to the application. The n-grams typically are collected from a text or speech corpus. When the items are words, n-grams may also be called shingles.[1]  An n-gram of size 1 is referred to as a \"unigram\"; size 2 is a \"bigram\" (or, less commonly, a \"digram\"); size 3 is a \"trigram\". Larger sizes are sometimes referred to by the value of n, e.g., \"four-gram\", \"five-gram\", and so on.","topics":[],"score":2300},{"name":"ada-carter/BeetleTracker","owner":"ada-carter","html_url":"https://github.com/ada-carter/BeetleTracker","stars":0,"forks":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":2300},{"name":"mremigio331/FortunasBetLambdas","owner":"mremigio331","html_url":"https://github.com/mremigio331/FortunasBetLambdas","stars":0,"forks":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":2300},{"name":"alevenberg/tic-tac-toe","owner":"alevenberg","html_url":"https://github.com/alevenberg/tic-tac-toe","stars":0,"forks":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"A CLI tic tac toe game","topics":[],"score":2300},{"name":"BryanCW0303/Leetcode","owner":"BryanCW0303","html_url":"https://github.com/BryanCW0303/Leetcode","stars":0,"forks":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":2300},{"name":"abdulrahman1121/linkedin-insight","owner":"abdulrahman1121","html_url":"https://github.com/abdulrahman1121/linkedin-insight","stars":0,"forks":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":2300},{"name":"vickiekknight/